/* alpha1 (decision 0244): API-call recorder and desktop probe for the NATIVE build. TEST TOOL, not product code: link-time wrappers (-Wl,--wrap=fle_imp_NAME, generated by gen-wrap.py), nothing in the runtime changes.
 * Forked from pick1's apiw_core.c (decision 0242) and extended with the arguments that matter for translucency: BLENDFUNCTION of UpdateLayeredWindow(Indirect)/AlphaBlend, dwFlags, crKey, positions, the premultiplication state of the source
 * bitmap of a UpdateLayeredWindow, DWM_BLURBEHIND, MARGINS, AnimateWindow, GradientFill, BufferedPaint, and the class name of the window of each call.
 * Output $A1_OUT (default /dev/null):
 *   "E MS NAME cls=CLASS ARGS ra=.. ret=.."   one row per call of an event API, in order (MS = the virtual clock)
 *   "P NAME COUNT ARGS ret=.."                probe rows (capability queries; distinct arguments + return value), written at each dump
 *   "A NAME COUNT"                            calls of every import since the previous dump
 * At every `cpu LABEL` line of a G3 native script (the harness calls getrusage; this file wraps getrusage) it also: composes the desktop with fle_desk_compose() (what the page would show), writes "#dump N clock_ms MS", the
 * fle_desk_describe() text ("D ..." lines), the premultiplication statistics of the 4th byte of every top-level window surface ("W ..." lines), the pixels at the points of $A1_PIX ("x,y;x,y;..." -> "S N x y r g b a" of the composed desktop),
 * and the raw RGBA crops of $A1_CROP ("x,y,w,h;..." -> $A1_DIR/crop-NNNN-K.rgba).
 * THE INPUT IS A HARNESS SIMULATION (G3 script), NOT A USER OPERATION. */
